<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Yanjun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/935">935</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Huizong of Min</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Yanjun was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-shenzhi">Wang Shenzhi</a>, founder of the Min kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a>. He seized power in 926 and in 933 proclaimed himself emperor, breaking with the northern dynasties, but his extravagant rule ended when he was murdered in a palace coup in 935, the first of a series of killings among the Min rulers.</p></div>
